# Dotfiles

Personal dotfiles managed as a bare git repository.

## Quick Install

# Add user
**One-liner (as root):**
```bash
USERNAME=aibot &&
useradd -m -s /bin/bash "$USERNAME" &&
usermod -aG sudo "$USERNAME" &&
passwd "$USERNAME" &&
# optional ssh key copy:
[ -f /root/.ssh/authorized_keys ] && {
    cp -r /root/.ssh "/home/$USERNAME/" &&
    chown -R "$USERNAME:$USERNAME" "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh" &&
    chmod 700 "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh" &&
    chmod 600 "/home/$USERNAME/.ssh/"*
}
```

# Install as user
```bash
# One-liner (requires git and curl)
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles/master/.local/bin/install-dotfiles.sh | bash
```

Or clone and run manually:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles.git /tmp/dotfiles
bash /tmp/dotfiles/.local/bin/install-dotfiles.sh
```

### Installation Options

```bash
# Install without extra software (just dotfiles)
./install-dotfiles.sh --no-extras

# Use HTTPS instead of SSH (if you don't have SSH keys set up)
./install-dotfiles.sh --https

# Show help
./install-dotfiles.sh --help
```

## What Gets Installed

### Base Dependencies
- git, tmux, curl, zsh, wget, ripgrep

### Optional Software (use --no-extras to skip)
- [starship](https://starship.rs/) - Cross-shell prompt
- [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) - Fast Python package manager
- [nvm](https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm) + Node.js
- [neovim](https://neovim.io/) - Latest release
- [go](https://go.dev/) - Latest release

## Manual Installation

If you prefer to install manually or the script doesn't work for your system:

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
sudo apt install git tmux curl zsh wget ripgrep  # Debian/Ubuntu
# sudo dnf install git tmux curl zsh wget ripgrep  # Fedora
# sudo pacman -S git tmux curl zsh wget ripgrep    # Arch

# 2. Clone dotfiles as bare repo
git clone --bare https://github.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles.git $HOME/.cfg

# 3. Define the config alias
alias config='/usr/bin/git --git-dir=$HOME/.cfg/ --work-tree=$HOME'

# 4. Ignore the bare repo directory
echo ".cfg" >> $HOME/.gitignore

# 5. Checkout the files (backup any conflicts first!)
config checkout

# 6. Hide untracked files in status
config config --local status.showUntrackedFiles no

# 7. Change shell to zsh
chsh -s $(which zsh)

# 8. Install optional software
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
curl -sS https://starship.rs/install.sh | sh
curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.40.4/install.sh | bash

# 9. Install Go (latest)
GO_VERSION=$(curl -sL 'https://go.dev/VERSION?m=text' | head -1)
wget "https://go.dev/dl/${GO_VERSION}.linux-amd64.tar.gz"
tar -xzf "${GO_VERSION}.linux-amd64.tar.gz"
mv go ~/.local/go
ln -sf ~/.local/go/bin/go ~/.local/bin/go
ln -sf ~/.local/go/bin/gofmt ~/.local/bin/gofmt
```

## Usage

After installation, use the `config` alias to manage dotfiles:

```bash
config status                    # Check status
config add ~/.config/nvim/init.lua   # Stage a file
config commit -m "Update nvim config"  # Commit
config push                      # Push to remote
```

## Creating a New User with Dotfiles

Use the included helper script to create a new user with SSH access:

```bash
# Create user only
~/.local/bin/create-user.sh john

# Create user and set up full environment
~/.local/bin/create-user.sh john --with-setup
```

## Fresh Server Setup (SSH as root)

When you SSH into a new server as root and want to create a user with dotfiles:

**1. Create the user (as root):**
```bash
useradd -m -s /bin/bash <username>
usermod -aG sudo <username>
passwd <username>

# Copy SSH keys to new user
mkdir -p /home/<username>/.ssh
cp ~/.ssh/authorized_keys /home/<username>/.ssh/
chmod 700 /home/<username>/.ssh
chmod 600 /home/<username>/.ssh/authorized_keys
chown -R <username>:<username> /home/<username>/.ssh
```

**2. SSH as the new user and install dotfiles:**
```bash
ssh <username>@<server> -A

# Run the install script
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles/master/.local/bin/install-dotfiles.sh | bash

# Or with HTTPS if GitHub SSH isn't set up
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexander-bech/dotfiles/master/.local/bin/install-dotfiles.sh | bash -s -- --https
```


## Structure

```
~/.config/
    nvim/          # Neovim configuration
    zsh/           # Zsh configuration
    tmux/          # Tmux configuration
    starship.toml  # Starship prompt config
    shell/         # Shell profile and aliases
    ...

~/.local/bin/      # Personal scripts
```

## Troubleshooting

### "SSH connection failed" during clone
Use the `--https` flag or set up SSH keys:
```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub  # Add to GitHub
```

### Conflicting files
The installer backs up conflicts to `~/.dotfiles-backup-<timestamp>/`

### Shell not changing
Log out and back in, or run `exec zsh`

### Starship not loading
Ensure `~/.local/bin` is in your PATH and restart your shell

## Delete User

```bash
sudo deluser --remove-home username
```
